  "description": "QEHBUD crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C176 H156 Nd4 O26. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.606-4.113 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.53-118.10°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C188H184Nd4O26. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
